# Database dumps. `scripts/backup.sh dump` writes here by default, and a dump
# holds every seller's scrypt hash, every sealed eBay token, every buyer's chat
# and the whole audit chain. It must never be committable — and this was NOT
# ignored when the first dump was taken, so one `git add -A` would have done it.
# `backup.sh` refuses to write into a directory git would not ignore.
/backups/
*.sql.gz
